### Area 4: the audit viewer. Read-only over the hash-chained trail.
### Sign in first (requests/auth.http). Every route needs audit.read: SYSTEM_ADMIN
### and AUDITOR hold it. Any other role gets 403 FORBIDDEN with a traceId, and the
### refusal is audited. There is no route that writes, edits or deletes an event.
@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000

### Newest events first. Filters are optional and combine with "and":
### actorKind (user, system, ai), actorUserId, role, action (starts with),
### entityType, entityId, from and to (ISO times, inclusive), refusalsOnly,
### search (words in the summary), page and pageSize (1 to 200).
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/audit/events?pageSize=10

### Only refusals: a refused sign-in, permission, CSRF check or reused token.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/audit/events?refusalsOnly=true

### The history of one record. This is what an operation log under a record reads.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/audit/events?entityType=User&entityId=paste-a-user-id-here

### A time range, and everything under one action prefix.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/audit/events?action=governance.&from=2026-11-01T00:00:00.000Z&to=2026-11-30T23:59:59.999Z

### One event, with its changes masked for your role.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/audit/events/paste-an-event-id-here

### Walk the whole chain: verified up to a sequence, or broken at one.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/audit/chain
